# Cloudflare Workers static-assets headers.
# https://developers.cloudflare.com/workers/static-assets/headers
# https://opennext.js.org/cloudflare/caching#static-assets-caching
#
# Next.js content-hashes every file under /_next/static, so the bytes behind a
# given URL never change — they are safe to cache forever. Without this, Workers
# Assets serves them `cache-control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate`
# (cf-cache MISS on every request), so each SPA page load re-fetches ~20 chunks
# from the worker origin. That drove both the CF cost (the "Wave 32" rate-limit
# rule's motivation) AND — until the rule was scoped to exclude static assets —
# the per-load 429 burst that crashed sign-in/up. Immutable edge caching fixes
# the root: chunks become cf-cache HITs and stop hitting the origin.
/_next/static/*
  Cache-Control: public,max-age=31536000,immutable
